Worldprint for the Psion Series3a by M.Schuster in 1994

EMail: ns103@fim.uni-erlangen.de


This little hack is look-, fun- and FREEware .. ;-)


Ever wondered why Psion displays the world in the world.app only as a
b/w-image without grey? I don't know, but here is a little prg. which
will show you how nice the map could be shown .. 

It loads the world-map from ROM:: .. then you can choose, how you want
the world displayed:

1. shadow .. prints the worldmap in grey with a black shadow. Choose
   the 'height' between shadow an map. This is very very simple and looks
   much more better then an b/w-image.
   
2. 3d .. prints the world on bottom&right borders with a black and on
   upper&left borders with a white border-line. (Excuse me, but I don't
   know how I should describe this ;-) )
   You can choose if you want a grey or a light grey background.
   
3. relief .. prints the world as a relief. You can choose if you want
   the relief-lines up or down (same excuse as 2. - the one looks
   like the line is over the screen (up), the other looks like the line
   is stamped into the screen (down) ) .. also you can choose if you want
   a grey or a light grey background...
   

So, just have a look at it.. (i guess you think "my god, haven't he got
something else to programme?!" ..i have, and i have more I could do, but
sometimes I had to do something short, nice, ... :-) )


